000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0000\u0013 SEQ CHAPTER \\h \\r 1\u0015MINUTES OF A REGULAR MEETING OF\rTHE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF CALABASAS,\rCALIFORNIA, HELD WEDNESDAY, MARCH 10, 2010\r\rMayor Wolfson called the meeting to order at 7:02 p.m. in the City Council Chambers, 100 Civic Center Way, Calabasas, California.\r\rROLL CALL Present: Mayor Wolfson, Mayor pro Tem Groveman, Councilmembers Bozajian, Maurer and Washburn.\r Absent: None.\r Staff: Bingham, Colantuono, Coroalles, Davidoo, Mirzakhanian, Parker, Peirce, Starns, Tamuri, Yalda.\r \r The Pledge of Allegiance was led by Bette Hall. \r\rAPPROVAL OF AGENDA\r \rCouncilmember Maurer moved, seconded by Mayor pro Tem Groveman, to approve the agenda. MOTION CARRIED 5/0. \r\rANNOUNCEMENTS/INTRODUCTIONS \r\rMayor Wolfson introduced Bette Hall, President of the Calabasas Rotary Club, who spoke regarding 2010 Nuts for Mutts 5k Walk on April 18, 2010. Mayor Wolfson presented proclamations to members of the School Area Traffic Safety 2010 Teen Advisory Committee in recognition of their service to the Committee. Councilmember Bozajian announced that the Open House Celebration will be held at the Agoura/Calabasas Community Center on March 13 and that the Annual Eggstravaganza will be held on April 3. Councilmember Maurer announced that the City�s Annual Arbor Day Celebration will be taking place on March 20. Mayor Wolfson reminded everyone that Daylight Saving Time will be ending on March 14 and spoke regarding upcoming electronic waste and hazardous waste collection events.\r\rORAL COMMUNICATIONS - PUBLIC COMMENT \r\r Arin Mikailian, Glendale, spoke regarding the upcoming release of \u0013 HYPERLINK \"http://www.calabasas.hatch.com\" \u0014www.calabasas.hatch.com\u0015, which will be a loca